    "logic": {
      "concept": "A trend-continuation entry for a market that grinds rather than spikes. The EMA(30)/EMA(200) ribbon says which side is permitted; a close pushing through the Keltner band (EMA(20) +/- 2.0 x ATR(14)) is the entry event; and a trailing ATR stop with no target lets the drift run. Note for whoever reads the Q3 audit first: a channel break in a low-volatility regime is often the START of the market leaving Q3 for Q1, and that is expected. Trades are attributed by their ENTRY bar, never the exit, so a position opened in Q3 that earns all of its profit inside Q1 still scores as a Q3 trade under Gate R.",
      "entry": "LONG when Close > EMA(30) > EMA(200) and Close crosses ABOVE EMA(20) + 2.0 x ATR(14). SHORT mirrors it: Close < EMA(30) < EMA(200) and Close crosses BELOW EMA(20) - 2.0 x ATR(14).",
      "exit": "The trailing stop at 4.0 x ATR(14), ratcheting behind the best price seen since the fill, or Close crossing back through EMA(30) - whichever the bar reaches first. No take-profit is modelled (tp_atr_mult=None)."
    }
  },
